<div class="block d-block" id="block-ncei-page-title"><h1><span property="schema:name">Conductivity, Temperature and Depth (CTD) data from KAIMALINO, WECOMA and other platforms in the TOGA Area - Pacific from 1988-10-30 to 1991-12-09 (NCEI Accession 9500039)</span></h1></div>
<h2></h2>
<div class="block d-block" id="block-ncei-content"><div property="schema:text" class="clearfix text-formatted">
<div class="row">
<div class="col-xs-4 col-sm-3 col-md-2">
<a href="/access/metadata/landing-page/bin/gfx?id=gov.noaa.nodc:9500039"><img alt="browse graphic" class=" img-responsive " src="/access/metadata/landing-page/bin/gfx?id=gov.noaa.nodc:9500039"></a><small>Graphic not available.</small>
</div>
<div class="col-md-7 abstract">The multiple sets of Conductivity, Temperature and Depth (CTD) data were collected in TOGA Area - Pacific (30 N to 30 S) as part of World Ocean Circulation Experiment (WOCE). Data was collected from ships A. AGASSIZ, MOANA WAVE, WECOMA, KAIMALINO by principal investigators from different Institutions. The data was collected over a period spanning from October 30, 1988 to December 9, 1991. Data was submitted by Steven M. Chiswell of Bundesamt für Seeschifffahrt und Hydrographie, Hamburg, Germany.</div>
